feat(credentials): resolve the API key through the host credential seam

The plugin only understood an environment-variable name, so the key could not be
entered anywhere the user could reach — which is not how any other keyed plugin
in this harness works. It now resolves the credential per evaluation through
ctx.credentials when that service is mounted, and falls back to the process
environment when it is not.

Resolution is deliberately per call rather than cached at activation: the
credential seam is writable while the host runs, so a key saved from the
settings page has to reach the very next tool call without a restart.

That also changes when the plugin is allowed to fail. With a credential seam
mounted the settings page is a real configuration path, so activation succeeds
and an unset key fails the call that needs it, naming the reference. Without the
seam the environment is the only source and activation stays the earliest point
it can be judged, so a missing key still fails there.

The narrow local contract is safe because the seam brands references with a
compile-time-only brand (brandString returns its argument unchanged); the
reference grammar is restated locally so a malformed apiKeyEnv reads as unset
rather than throwing inside the provider.

Also: validation moves to src/jev/validation.ts, and the browser manifest
declares the remotes carrier the settings page needs.
